:"shealtiel_2456","name":"Shealtiel","also":"Salathiel","summary":"Asked for of God, father of Zerubbabel (Ezra 3:2, 8; Neh. 12:1).","verses":11,"father":"Jehoiachin","mother":"","v":[2,8]},{"id":"cyrus_968","name":"Cyrus","also":"","summary":"(Heb. Ko’resh), the celebrated “King of Persia” (Elam) who was conqueror of Babylon, and issued the decree of liberation to the Jews (Ezra 1:1, 2).","verses":19,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"jeshua_895","name":"Jeshua","also":"","summary":"Ezra 2:40; Neh. 7:43.","verses":8,"father":"Azaniah","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"kadmiel_1767","name":"Kadmiel","also":"","summary":"Before God; i.e., his servant, one of the Levites who returned with Zerubbabel from the Captivity (Neh. 9:4; 10:9; 12:8).","verses":8,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"hodevah_1542","name":"Hodevah","also":"Judah, Hodaviah","summary":"","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"henadad_1493","name":"Henadad","also":"","summary":"Favour of Hadad, the name of a Levite after the Captivity (Ezra 3:9).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"asaph_330","name":"Asaph","also":"","summary":"A Levite; one of the leaders of David’s choir (1 Chr. 6:39). Psalms 50 and 73-83 inclusive are attributed to him. He is mentioned along with David as skilled in music, and a “seer” (2 Chr. 29:30).","verses":32,"father":"Berechiah","mother":"","v":[10]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,8]},{"id":"joppa_652","name":"Joppa","kind":"City","lat":32.05372,"lon":34.75212,"summary":"Beauty, a town in the portion of Dan (Josh. 19:46; A.V., “Japho”), on a sandy promontory between Caesarea and Gaza, and at a distance of 30 miles north-west from Jerusalem.","verses":14,"v":[7]},{"id":"lebanon_720","name":"Lebanon","kind":"Region","lat":33.92154,"lon":35.89897,"summary":"White, “the white mountain of Syria,” is the loftiest and most celebrated mountain range in Syria. It is a branch running southward from the Caucasus, and at its lower end forking into two parallel ranges, the eastern or Anti-Lebanon, and the western or Lebanon proper.","verses":56,"v":[7]},{"id":"persia_938","name":"Persia","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":34.79831,"lon":48.51497,"summary":"An ancient empire, extending from the Indus to Thrace, and from the Caspian Sea to the Red Sea and the Persian Gulf. The Persians were originally a Medic tribe which settled in Persia, on the eastern side of the Persian Gulf.","verses":25,"v":[7]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[7637,7637,7637,2320,1121,1121,5060,5060,5892,5892,5892,5971,5971,5971,622,259,259,376,413,3389],[3442,3442,1121,3136,3136,251,251,251,3548,2216,2216,2216,1121,7597,7597,251,251,251,6965,1129,1129,4196,4196,430,430,430,3478,3478,5927,5927,5930,5930,5921,5921,3789,3789,3789,3789,8451,8451,8451,4872,4872,376,376,430,430],[3559,3559,3559,4196,4196,5921,4350,4350,5927,5927,5930,5930,5921,5921,3068,3068,3068,1242,1242,6153,6153,5930,5930,3588,367,367,5971,5971,776,776,776],[6213,6213,6213,2282,2282,5521,5521,3789,3789,3789,3789,3789,3789,5930,5930,5930,5930,5930,3117,4557,4557,4557,4557,4941,3117,3117,3117],[310,310,8548,8548,8548,8548,5930,5930,2320,2320,2320,2320,2320,3605,3605,3605,4150,4150,6942,6942,3068,3068,3068,3605,3605,3605,3605,5071,5071,5071,5068,3068,3068,3068],[259,259,259,3117,7637,7637,7637,2320,2490,2490,2490,5927,5927,5930,5930,3068,3068,3068,1964,1964,1964,1964,1964,1964,3068,3068,3068,3245,3245,3245,3245],[5414,5414,3701,2